data: {"choices":[{"delta":{"tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"\"content\": \"# Dispatch to developer — implement DESIGN.md\\n\\nImplement the design and commit it, per your brief (roles/developer.md). One pass,\\nnothing held back.\\n\\nThe design is in your clone already: I have pushed my HEAD, and it sits at\\n`refs/campaign/orchestrator` (commit 3cd2423). Bring it into your branch with:\\n\\n    git merge refs/campaign/orchestrator\\n\\nthen read `DESIGN.md` at the repository root and build exactly what it says.\\n\\nSummary of what DESIGN.md specifies (the file is authoritative):\\n\\n- A React + Vite single page: greeting `Hello, world!` as an `h1`, with three\\n  colour buttons beneath it (labels: Blue, Orange, Violet) that change the\\n  greeting's colour. State with `useState`.\\n- Everything from `@codesweep-ai/ui` (`npm install @codesweep-ai/ui`, latest):\\n  wrap the page in `AppShell`, place its `Header` (title \\\"Colour Greeting\\\", no\\n  nav, no actions) and its `Footer` (text \\\"Built with the codesweep design\\n  system\\\") inside, use its `Button` (`variant=\\\"secondary\\\"`, `size=\\\"md\\\"`) for the\\n  three buttons.\\n- Greeting colours are the tokens `--color-cat-1` (Blue, the default on load),\\n  `--color-cat-6` (Orange), `--color-cat-5` (Violet). No hex values anywhere.\\n- Layout: header top, footer bottom; greeting centred horizontally with the\\n  button row centred beneath it, the group vertically centred in the content\\n  area.\\n- Import the styles once at the entry point: `styles/core.css`,\\n  `styles/components/app-shell.css`, `styles/components/button.css`.\\n\\nPer your brief, also: bind the dev server to `0.0.0.0` port 5173; write\\n`README.md` at the repo root naming the build command and the serve command;\\nwrite `.gitignore` holding `node_modules/` and `dist/` before your first commit;\\nleave the optional peers (`mermaid`, `puppeteer`, `pixelmatch`, `pngjs`) out.\\n\\nCommit everything to your own branch. Then reply reporting the branch you\\ncommitted to and the two commands you documented.\\n"},"index":0}]},"finish_reason":null,"index":0,"raw_output":null}],"created":1793342853,"id":"chatcmpl-fe8322a3","model":"accounts/fireworks/models/kimi-k3","object":"chat.completion.chunk","usage":null}

